%N A105192 Number of divisors of n101.
%H A105192 Chris R. Rehmann, <a href="/A105192/b105192.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%e A105192 If n=0, then the number of divisors of 0101 is 2 (since it is a prime).
%p A105192 a:= n-> numtheory[tau](parse(cat(n,"101"))):
%p A105192 seq(a(n), n=0..111);  # _Alois P. Heinz_, Oct 28 2026
%t A105192 DivisorSigma[0, Range[0, 100]*1000 + 101] (* _Paolo Xausa_, Oct 28 2026 *)
%o A105192 (MATLAB) N = 111; a = arrayfun(@(n) prod(groupcounts(factor(1000*n+101)')+1),0:min(N-1,flintmax)); disp(strjoin(string(a),', ')) % _Chris R. Rehmann_, Oct 28 2026
